{"author":"rebar-bridge[bot]","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1794264620111813002,"compiled_state":{"alias":"lovely-bipartisan-mullet","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":4,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"c8b9211a094f2cdc59a80b3f5be2cd9a117b284d5872d2bbab62768569da786a","event_uuid":"4b593d0b-58e2-47e6-9502-30a7a5df8946","position":{"commit_sha":"20fd25d8c05d4687de805a7f029903cb632b1a86","position":"1794256406426801001-4b593d0b-58e2-47e6-9502-30a7a5df8946"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"},{"content_hash":"8ccc78bd3a7e0d3e26ab4e88259fe41a4a6c1b38ea4f7dde949ce6406b14e12c","event_uuid":"27cf758e-cdde-4fa5-9251-8d35b325a9bf","position":{"commit_sha":"42f1f9abbb7b0f71c5fde093aaf8ba916369c064","position":"1794256632685069001-27cf758e-cdde-4fa5-9251-8d35b325a9bf"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"},{"content_hash":"863e75459163b84b1c5fcfb35f4ffaf472649e304b115f6e472878f326c84fa1","event_uuid":"d9a605d5-e8f9-4988-813a-32312ffaa115","position":{"commit_sha":"7a4ebc7fe82076516dbfeedff4b2ed62e2ba61f1","position":"1794256766773490001-d9a605d5-e8f9-4988-813a-32312ffaa115"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"},{"content_hash":"2dda5fad006ee082ea9674b53e027c2f6318ea09375b9b142d679dca430c0823","event_uuid":"7da1bee6-cb6e-434c-b25d-a402cfa83fe0","position":{"commit_sha":"bd7900768c52fcf1d5f59cbd65c8a3f786e31502","position":"1794264620111813001-7da1bee6-cb6e-434c-b25d-a402cfa83fe0"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1794256406426801001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"d9a605d5-e8f9-4988-813a-32312ffaa115","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"3a2b-a8db-d642-44ab"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nAfter the reducer child, rebar can store `releases` but the bridge never reads Jira's `fixVersions`: the Cloud search requests a fixed field list without it (`src/rebar/reconciler/adapters/jira/acli.py:238-251`), no inbound differ compares it, and no applier writes it. So a fix version a team sets in Jira never reaches the bound rebar ticket. This child implements the Jira→rebar direction designed in ADR 0124 (decisions 3, 4 and 7), following the labels→tags path.\n\n## Approach\n\n1. **Fetch.** Add `\"fixVersions\"` to the Cloud search field list in `src/rebar/reconciler/adapters/jira/acli.py` (lines 241-250). The Data Center adapter needs no fetch change: its `search_issues` passes no `fields` argument to pycontribs (`src/rebar/reconciler/adapters/jira_datacenter/_issues.py:199-205`, called page by page from `fetch_paging.py:91`), and pycontribs `JIRA.search_issues` maps an omitted or `None` `fields` to `[\"*all\"]` (pycontribs/jira `jira/client.py`, `search_issues`); the DC test below pins that `fixVersions` survives `_unwrap`. The bound-but-absent direct GET (`get_issue_by_rest`, `acli_rest.py:325-333`) already returns all fields.\n2. **Diff.** Add `_diff_releases_inbound(jira_fields, local_ticket)` to `src/rebar/reconciler/inbound_collection_diffs.py` beside `_diff_labels_inbound` (lines 194-214). It reads the names from `jira_fields[\"fixVersions\"]` (a list of version objects; take each dict's `name`, skip entries without a string name), set-diffs them against `local_ticket[\"releases\"]`, and returns sorted `{\"action\": \"add\"|\"remove\", \"release\": name}` records. Observation guard: when `\"fixVersions\"` is absent from `jira_fields`, or is not a list, return `[]`, so a snapshot that never fetched the field cannot be read as \"all releases removed\". This mirrors the G1 guard in `_diff_link_removals_inbound` (same file, lines 168-172).\n3. **Mutation.** Add a `releases` list field to `InboundMutation` (`src/rebar/reconciler/inbound_differ.py:60-70`), compute it in `compute_inbound_mutations` (line 289 onward), and include it in the emit condition (line 353). To keep `compute_inbound_mutations` within its complexity ceiling, first extract the existing label-suppression block (lines 308-322) into a behavior-preserving helper `_suppress_collection_echoes(mutations, adds, removes, key)`; the outbound child reuses it for releases. Carry `\"releases\"` through `run_differs.py` (the inbound typed-payload dict at lines 365-380) and add it to `InboundUpdatePayload` and `_INBOUND_UPDATE_KEYS` in `src/rebar/reconciler/mutation_payloads.py` (lines 264-301).\n4. **Apply.** In `src/rebar/reconciler/apply_inbound_events.py`, extract the read-state/no-op-suppression/add-wins-dedup body of `_inbound_update_apply_labels` (lines 322-389) into a shared `_apply_inbound_list_delta(...)` parameterized by payload key, entry key, state key and event type, and call it for labels (`TAG_DELTA`, unchanged behavior) and for releases (`RELEASE_DELTA`). Both write `source=\"inbound\"` and both skip the write when the reducer fails or returns `None`. Call the release applier from `apply_inbound.py` next to the labels call (line 133).\n5. **Contract.** Register `\"releases\": FieldSymmetry(name=\"releases\", symmetry=ADD_WINS, conflict_class=\"set\", outbound_name=\"fixVersions\", codec=\"Jira fixVersions[].name ↔ local 'releases'\", notes=...)` in `src/rebar/reconciler/_field_contract.py`, and `\"releases\": \"set\"` in `conflict_resolver.FIELD_CLASSES` (`src/rebar/reconciler/conflict_resolver.py:28-39`). The import-time guard in `tests/unit/reconciler/test_field_contract_properties.py:32-52` then covers it.\n6. **Docs.** Add a \"Fix versions ↔ releases\" row to the sync-semantics table in `docs/jira-sync-setup.md` (section \"Sync semantics & limitations\", line 321), marking inbound supported and outbound as delivered by the next child, and pointing to ADR 0124.\n\nImported tickets: the inbound CREATE path is unchanged. A ticket created from a Jira issue gets its releases on the following pass through the bound-ticket update diff, so no CREATE body change and no second CREATE writer.\n\nSafety while only this direction exists: no local writer of `RELEASE_DELTA` exists until the surfaces child, so the inbound set-diff cannot strip a locally intended release. The surfaces child depends on the outbound child for that reason.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/reconciler/adapters/jira/acli.py`\n- `src/rebar/reconciler/inbound_collection_diffs.py`\n- `src/rebar/reconciler/inbound_differ.py`\n- `src/rebar/reconciler/run_differs.py`\n- `src/rebar/reconciler/mutation_payloads.py`\n- `src/rebar/reconciler/apply_inbound_events.py`\n- `src/rebar/reconciler/apply_inbound.py`\n- `src/rebar/reconciler/_field_contract.py`\n- `src/rebar/reconciler/conflict_resolver.py`\n- `docs/jira-sync-setup.md`\n- `tests/unit/reconciler/diffing/test_inbound_releases.py` (new)\n- `tests/unit/reconciler/mutate/test_inbound_apply_releases.py` (new)\n- `tests/unit/reconciler/test_field_contract_properties.py` (extend)\n- `tests/unit/reconciler/fetch/test_fetcher_snapshot.py` (extend: Cloud field list)\n- `tests/unit/reconciler/test_dc_backend_characterization.py` (extend: DC payload keeps `fixVersions`)\n\n## Testing\n\nPayload fixtures use the documented version object shape (`{\"self\",\"id\",\"name\",\"archived\",\"released\"}`, Jira Cloud OpenAPI `Version`), because no project on the production site has a version to record (ADR 0124 Evidence).\n- Diff: Jira `[{\"name\":\"2.4\"},{\"name\":\"2.5\"}]` vs local `[\"2.4\",\"old\"]` yields add `2.5`, remove `old`; equal sets yield `[]`; `fixVersions` absent yields `[]` even when local has releases; a malformed entry (no name, non-dict) is skipped.\n- Apply: an update mutation with release add/remove writes exactly one `RELEASE_DELTA` with `source=\"inbound\"`; a repeat with the state already matching writes nothing; a reducer exception writes nothing; a mutation with both add and remove of one name writes it as added only. Existing label-apply tests pass unchanged (they pin the extraction).\n- Cloud fetch requests `fixVersions`; a DC search payload carrying `fixVersions` reaches the snapshot with names intact.\n- Contract: `FIELD_CONTRACT[\"releases\"]` is `ADD_WINS`/`set`, and `process_release_delta` keeps a name both added and removed in one event (add-wins property, mirroring the labels property test).\n- Two passes over the same Jira payload: the first writes one `RELEASE_DELTA`, the second writes nothing.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A bound Jira issue whose `fixVersions` gain or lose a name produces one `RELEASE_DELTA` (`source=\"inbound\"`) with that delta on the bound ticket, for both Cloud- and DC-shaped payloads; pinned by the tests above.\n- [ ] A repeat pass with no Jira change writes no event, and a snapshot without the `fixVersions` key never removes local releases; pinned by tests.\n- [ ] `FIELD_CONTRACT` and `conflict_resolver.FIELD_CLASSES` both register `releases` (`ADD_WINS`, `set`), and `tests/unit/reconciler/test_field_contract_properties.py` passes with the new add-wins case.\n- [ ] Existing label inbound tests in `tests/unit/reconciler/` pass unchanged.\n- [ ] `docs/jira-sync-setup.md` lists the fix-versions row.\n- [ ] `python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check` and `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --check` both exit 0, and no `src/rebar` file exceeds 800 lines.\n- [ ] `env -u JIRA_URL -u JIRA_USER -u JIRA_API_TOKEN make verify` exits 0 on the commit pushed for review.","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/reconciler/adapters/jira/acli.py","reason":"fetch fixVersions"},{"path":"src/rebar/reconciler/inbound_collection_diffs.py","reason":"release diff"},{"path":"src/rebar/reconciler/inbound_differ.py","reason":"mutation field and suppression helper"},{"path":"src/rebar/reconciler/run_differs.py","reason":"payload plumbing"},{"path":"src/rebar/reconciler/mutation_payloads.py","reason":"inbound payload key"},{"path":"src/rebar/reconciler/apply_inbound_events.py","reason":"RELEASE_DELTA writer"},{"path":"src/rebar/reconciler/apply_inbound.py","reason":"call release applier"},{"path":"src/rebar/reconciler/_field_contract.py","reason":"register releases"},{"path":"src/rebar/reconciler/conflict_resolver.py","reason":"FIELD_CLASSES"},{"path":"docs/jira-sync-setup.md","reason":"sync table row"},{"path":"tests/unit/reconciler/diffing/test_inbound_releases.py","reason":"new"},{"path":"tests/unit/reconciler/mutate/test_inbound_apply_releases.py","reason":"new"},{"path":"tests/unit/reconciler/test_field_contract_properties.py","reason":"add-wins case"},{"path":"tests/unit/reconciler/fetch/test_fetcher_snapshot.py","reason":"Cloud field list"},{"path":"tests/unit/reconciler/test_dc_backend_characterization.py","reason":"DC payload"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["depends_on","3a2b-a8db-d642-44ab"],["parent","21ec-3e9b-4a27-4775"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"21ec-3e9b-4a27-4775","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"50aa-b7a1-e9a1-44ac","ticket_type":"story","title":"Sync Jira fixVersions into rebar releases (inbound)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["4b593d0b-58e2-47e6-9502-30a7a5df8946","27cf758e-cdde-4fa5-9251-8d35b325a9bf","d9a605d5-e8f9-4988-813a-32312ffaa115","7da1bee6-cb6e-434c-b25d-a402cfa83fe0"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1794264620111813002,"uuid":"f074ff54-083f-4c4b-a33c-878e34285554"}